- whisper.cpp (https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp), v1.9.5, MIT, Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The
  ggml authors: built into the app from third_party/whisper.cpp for on-device voice typing.
  app/src/main/cpp/ribbit_whisper.c is adapted from its examples/whisper.android JNI code.
- OpenAI Whisper model weights (https://github.com/openai/whisper), MIT, in ggml form from
  https://huggingface.co/ggerganov/whisper.cpp: downloaded at build time and shipped in the APK.
- Material Design icons by Google (https://github.com/google/material-design-icons), Apache
  License 2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0): the send, stop, add, tune and mic
  glyph paths in app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_send.xml, ic_stop.xml, ic_new.xml, ic_settings.xml and
  ic_mic.xml.
- r1_escape (https://github.com/RabbitHoleEscapeR1/r1_escape): the MediaTek preloader FASTBOOT
  handshake that tools/enter-fastboot.py reimplements.
- TurboTheTurtle/rabbit-r1-firmware: R1 partition layout and hardware notes.
- Rabbit Inc.: official developer mode, the stock firmware images, and the flash sequence in its
  WebUSB flash tool, which tools/flash-stock.sh follows.
- Andy Yan's LineageOS GSI builds; mtkclient by B. Kerler (used, not included).

ribbitOS is not affiliated with Rabbit Inc. or the OpenClaw project. The repository contains no
firmware: stock rabbitOS and LineageOS images are downloaded by the user from their publishers.
